  "domain": "standards",
  "definition": "IEEE P2048-4 is the part of the IEEE 2048 virtual and augmented reality standards series that specifies immersive video file and stream formats: how classified immersive video content \u2014 360-degree, stereoscopic, and volumetric \u2014 is containerised, signalled, and delivered for storage and streaming across platforms. Where its sibling IEEE P2048-3 addresses who a user is in immersive environments (person identification), P2048-4 addresses how immersive media payloads are packaged and interchanged, defining metadata for projection type, viewport, and rendering parameters so content plays back correctly on heterogeneous devices.",
